-- statement:
--   For a complex Hilbert space H, WOTClosed(A) says a unital star subalgebra A of the bounded operators on H is closed in the weak operator topology, and wstar(S) is the infimum (intersection) of all weakly closed unital star subalgebras containing the operator set S. IsII1Factor(A) packages the following conditions: the zero operator differs from the identity, A is weakly closed, every element of A commuting with all of A is a scalar multiple of the identity, every isometry in A (star(v)v=1) is unitary, and every nonzero projection p in A has a nonzero proper subprojection q in A with pq=qp=q. HasSeparablePredual(A) means there is a separable complete complex normed space, in the same universe as H, whose strong dual is conjugate-linearly isometrically equivalent to A; no separability of H or of the operator norm topology is imposed. The ultraweak topology on operators is generated by the functionals T ↦ Σₙ ⟨xₙ, T yₙ⟩ for sequences with Σ‖xₙ‖‖yₙ‖ finite, and algebras carry the induced topology. IsNormalizedTrace(A,τ) asks a continuous linear functional τ on A to satisfy τ(1)=1, τ(x*x) has nonnegative real part, τ(x*)=conj τ(x), τ(xy)=τ(yx), faithfulness (τ(x*x)=0 forces x=0), and ultraweak continuity. traceDistance(τ,u,v) is the square root of the real part of τ((u−v)*(u−v)) for unitaries u,v of A, and traceTopology is the topology generated by open balls for this distance on the unitary group. relativeGeneratorLocus(B,A) is the set of unitaries u of A for which the weakly closed unital star algebra generated by B together with u equals A. MainTarget is a defined proposition, not an established theorem: for every Hilbert space H and every pair of subalgebras B ≤ A of operators on H that are both II₁ factors, if the relative commutant of B in A is only the scalars (an irreducible inclusion) and A has separable predual, then there exists a normalized faithful normal trace τ on A such that relativeGeneratorLocus(B,A) is both a Gδ set and dense in the unitary group of A under traceTopology.
